<title>USA: ABC taps Steve Burke as broadcast head - paper.</title>
<headline>ABC taps Steve Burke as broadcast head - paper.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Walt Disney Co's ABC has tapped Steve Burke for the position of president of broadcasting, Daily Variety said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Burke, 38, would oversee the company's radio group, television stations and Buena Vista TV syndication unit, the report said. He moved from a senior post at Walt Disney to ABC as an executive vice-president last year to help oversee ABC's transition to Disney ownership, he said.</p>
<p>He is the son of former Capital Cities-ABC CEO Dan Burke, Variety said.</p>
<p>((New York newsdesk 212-859-1610))</p>
